### The Numbers Don't Lie
759 recalls have been reported so far this year, with over a quarter classified as Class I--meaning a real risk to life or severe health consequences. Salmonella, allergens, and other contaminants are still making themselves unwelcome guests at our tables.

### Recent Recalls
Among the highlights--or lowlights--of the latest food safety alerts:

- **Spring & Mulberry Inc.**: Recall of date-sweetened chocolates due to Salmonella contamination. This repeat offender scored a chilling 96 on our failure scale.
  
- **Utz Quality Foods, LLC**: Multiple chip products suspect for Salmonella.
  
- **Champion Foods, LLC**: Bread products potentially contaminated with Salmonella.
  
- **George J Howe Company, Inc.**: Sunflower seeds recalled for undeclared tree nuts.
  
### Spotlight on Repeat Offenders
Spring & Mulberry Inc. is no stranger to the recall list, with 11 Class I incidents this year alone. The company continues to tarnish its reputation with each recall notice, so consider reconsidering those date-sweetened chocolates for your next snack.

### Are You Affected?
Check your pantry for products from the following brands: Joy Gourmet Foods LLC., Utz Quality Foods, Spring & Mulberry Inc., George J Howe Company, Inc., Champion Foods, LLC. If you have any of the recalled items, stop consuming them immediately.
